# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The asset tree powers sandboxed artifact iframes (`srcdoc`), which always run
# on an opaque `null` origin. Every request they make is therefore cross-origin
# and needs a wildcard CORS header — the same guarantee the ai4edu backend gave
# with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.
#
# Cloudflare Pages sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` for static assets by
# default, but relying on that implicitly is exactly how a working local build
# breaks in production. Stating it here makes the requirement explicit and
# survives any future change to the platform default.

/mb-assets/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  # Templates and their data files are immutable per deploy; the hashed Vite
  # bundle already caches itself.
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
